==English==

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|head=[[neck]] and neck|-}}

# very [[close]] in progress, as in a [[race]] or [[contest]]
#: {{ux|en|The polls suggest that the candidates were '''neck and neck''' in the election.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Love à-la-mode, etc.|author=Charles Macklin|page=20|year=1779|passage=It lay between me and Dick Riot madam; we were '''neck and neck''' for three miles, as hard as we could lay leg to ground, and running every inch, but at the first, I felt for him, found I had the foot {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|magazine=Sporting Magazine|passage=Mr. Prendergast's Rainbow filly, watched closely by Paul Jones, took the lead, and they ran almost '''neck and neck''' until near the cords, when Paul Jones made a rush, and came home by a length.|page=45|title=Sporting Intelligence|volkume=17|year=1825|month=November|issue=98}}
#: {{syn|en|nip and tuck}}

